# Workflow: Knowledge Sharing

Purpose:
  Enable knowledge sharing between AI agents and humans in the SDDRA system.
  Ensures that learned patterns, decisions, and skills are shared
  across the system and persist for future use.

## Knowledge Types

DECISIONS:
  What: Decision records (DEC-XXX.sdd)
  Where: .sdd/decisions/
  Sharing: All agents can read, only owner can write
  Retention: Permanent

SKILLS:
  What: Engineering skills (L1-L5)
  Where: .sdd/skills/
  Sharing: All agents can read and use
  Retention: Permanent, versioned

PATTERNS:
  What: Resilience and design patterns
  Where: .sdd/patterns/
  Sharing: All agents can read and use
  Retention: Permanent, versioned

WORKFLOWS:
  What: Execution workflows
  Where: .sdd/workflow/
  Sharing: All agents can read and use
  Retention: Permanent, versioned

MISTAKES:
  What: Lessons learned from failures
  Where: .sdd/decisions/ (as lessons)
  Sharing: All agents can read
  Retention: Permanent

CONTEXTS:
  What: Execution contexts and caches
  Where: .sdd/context/
  Sharing: Agents can read, system manages
  Retention: Temporary, cached

## Knowledge Sharing Mechanisms

### 1. Shared Registry

All agents share:
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing table)
  - .sdd/skills/INDEX.sdd (skill registry)
  - .sdd/decisions/INDEX.sdd (decision ledger)
  - .sdd/patterns/INDEX.sdd (pattern registry)

Access:
  - Read: All agents
  - Write: Only owner or authorized agents
  - Lock: Write operations are locked

### 2. Knowledge Extraction

When an agent learns something new:
  1. Identify knowledge type (decision, skill, pattern, mistake)
  2. Create appropriate file in .sdd/
  3. Add to registry
  4. Notify other agents
  5. Update indexes

Extraction Triggers:
  - New decision made
  - New pattern discovered
  - Mistake learned
  - Skill improved
  - Workflow optimized

### 3. Knowledge Distribution

Push Model:
  - Owner pushes changes to .sdd/
  - Agents detect changes via file watcher
  - Agents reload updated knowledge
  - Agents invalidate caches

Pull Model:
  - Agents periodically check .sdd/ for updates
  - Agents compare timestamps
  - Agents download changed files
  - Agents update local caches

Event Model:
  - Owner publishes knowledge update event
  - Agents subscribe to events
  - Agents receive notifications
  - Agents pull updates on notification

### 4. Knowledge Synchronization

Sync Points:
  - Before chain execution
  - After decision approval
  - After skill update
  - After pattern addition
  - Periodic (every N minutes)

Sync Process:
  1. Check for updates in .sdd/
  2. Compare with local cache
  3. Download changed files
  4. Validate changes
  5. Update local cache
  6. Notify agent components

## Knowledge Quality

Quality Metrics:
  - Relevance: How applicable to current project
  - Accuracy: How correct the knowledge is
  - Freshness: How recent the knowledge is
  - Usage: How often the knowledge is used

Quality Gates:
  - New skills must be validated before use
  - New decisions must be approved by human
  - New patterns must be reviewed
  - Mistakes must be documented with context

## Knowledge Sharing Workflow

New Knowledge:
  1. Agent discovers new pattern/decision/skill
  2. Agent creates .sdd/ file
  3. Agent adds to registry
  4. Agent notifies other agents
  5. Other agents update caches

Knowledge Update:
  1. Owner modifies .sdd/ file
  2. System detects change
  3. System validates change
  4. System notifies agents
  5. Agents update caches

Knowledge Retirement:
  1. Knowledge marked as DEPRECATED
  2. Dependent skills notified
  3. Migration path provided
  4. Knowledge archived after 6 months

## Runtime Knowledge Sharing

During Execution:
  - Agents share context via .sdd/context/
  - Agents read shared decisions
  - Agents use shared skills
  - Agents follow shared workflows

Between Sessions:
  - Knowledge persists in .sdd/
  - Sessions read from .sdd/
  - Sessions write to .sdd/ (with approval)
  - Knowledge accumulates over time

Between Projects:
  - .sdd/ can be copied to new project
  - Skills can be reused
  - Patterns can be reused
  - Decisions can be referenced

## Knowledge Sharing Commands

/sdd-share:
  Share knowledge with other agents
  Usage: /sdd-share --type=decision --id=DEC-100

/sdd-sync:
  Synchronize knowledge with remote
  Usage: /sdd-sync --direction=pull

/sdd-discover:
  Discover new knowledge from external sources
  Usage: /sdd-discover --source=old/external-repo-audit/

/sdd-audit:
  Audit knowledge quality
  Usage: /sdd-audit --type=skills

## Knowledge Governance

Ownership:
  - .sdd/ files: owned by human
  - Decisions: owned by human
  - Skills: owned by human
  - Patterns: owned by human

Access Control:
  - Read: All agents
  - Write: Owner only
  - Approve: Human only

Change Management:
  - All changes require DEC-XXX
  - Breaking changes require human approval
  - Deprecation requires 6-month notice

